MGA-Glide local patch 0116: the G200, G400 and G450 as PCI cards (GLOS D38).

86Box has the Matrox G-series only as AGP cards, and the 486 profiles have no
AGP slot, so they could have no Matrox card at all. The same devices on the
PCI bus: mystique_init() already adds a non-AGP card as an ordinary PCI one,
and its configuration space then has no AGP capability. The G200 reports
0520h, the PCI G200's device ID (0521h is the AGP one), and runs Matrox's PCI
G200 BIOS, 899-33, from the same package as the others (the AGP BIOS doesn't
know 0520h: it reported 2 MB and no framebuffer address). The G400 and G450
report 0525h either way, as on silicon, and keep their BIOSes. Matrox sold the
G200 and the G450 on PCI (the bench's G450 is one); the G400 PCI is here for
completeness.

